1
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:19,310
Who are you? Who the hell are you?

2
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:22,772
Isn't it obvious?

3
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:26,192
I'm Moon-jae.

4
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:27,569
Je Moon-jae.

5
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:32,657
Don't ever get caught by the cat.

6
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:34,659
It's really on edge right now.

7
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:39,247
You gotta stay alive
if you wanna find out who I am.

8
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,971
MOUSETRAP

9
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:15,635
Damn it.

10
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:18,680
Fuck.

11
00:02:19,722 --> 00:02:21,474
You wanna ride in the trunk?

12
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,853
- No.
- Let's just go quietly.

13
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:29,649
Okay.

14
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:42,203
What is it?

15
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:44,873
<i>You know that guy</i>
<i>we were looking for three years ago?</i>

16
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:49,169
The one we put all the card companies on?
What was his name? Je Moon-jae.

17
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,130
I just got a call
that a card in his name was used.

18
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:54,799
When?

19
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:55,925
<i>Just now.</i>

20
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:58,469
Hold on a second.

21
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:01,514
This bastard used the card again.

22
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,016
<i>He was quiet for three years.</i>

23
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,601
Now he's swiping everywhere.

24
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,227
Get me the location right away.

25
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:07,353
<i>Got it, Noja.</i>

26
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:13,943
Get out.

27
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,361
Sorry?

28
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:18,406
Go home and wait. I'll come back for you.

29
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:30,460
If I show up and you're not fucking there…

30
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:03,952
Huh? You little…

31
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:22,053
He moved out.

32
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:24,264
- When?
- Today.

33
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:27,892
He brought me this box of vitamin drinks
and thanked me for everything.

34
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:31,271
Then he came back,
acting like he didn't even remember.

35
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,649
He was just standing out there
staring into space,

36
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:37,235
then walked toward the market.

37
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:57,171
You fucking bastard.

38
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,653
Damn it.

39
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:42,342
If I catch you, you're fucking dead.

40
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:52,101
YONGHWADANG PHARMACY

41
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:56,230
Where is it?

42
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,570
Damn it.

43
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:33,142
<i>Don't ever get caught.</i>

44
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:36,854
You gotta stay alive
if you wanna find out who I am.

45
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:40,775
DANJINAE REAL ESTATE

46
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:48,908
Oh God!

47
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:51,786
Huh? You're that…

48
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:53,496
Let me see the contract.

49
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:59,877
Like I said, the contract was clean.

50
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,422
Just report it to the police.

51
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:05,216
Don't come complaining to us later.

52
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,762
You said he stole your apartment!

53
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:11,055
REAL ESTATE SALES CONTRACT

54
00:08:17,246 --> 00:08:19,373
Do not cross the police line!

55
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:26,506
The entire area is closed off tonight!

56
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:31,802
- Mr. Min.
- Yeah.

57
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:35,890
How long has it been?

58
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:37,975
DANGER: RISK OF COLLAPSE
DO NOT ENTER

59
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:45,816
Did you get the fingerprints?

60
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,734
Yes.

61
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:48,694
What's going on here?

62
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:50,238
Why are you here?

63
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:51,739
Hey.

64
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:53,074
Do you know him?

65
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:54,283
What's this?

66
00:08:56,118 --> 00:08:58,746
- Who said I'd know him?
- Violent Crimes Team 1 lead.

67
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:01,624
He said you handled their case
in Violent Crimes.

68
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:04,502
Heck, I wasn't even on his team anyway.

69
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:06,837
Why is he telling people stuff like that?

70
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:10,383
This bastard. He's Sang-cheol.

71
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:14,303
Illegal gambling, loan sharking,
stuff like that.

72
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:19,183
He killed someone over a gambling site
and fled to the Philippines.

73
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,269
- I think he's still there.
- And this guy?

74
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:24,897
- This bastard… I have no idea.
- Apparently, they're all in the same gang.

75
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:28,651
That gang fell apart years ago.
It was a total shitshow.

76
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:29,777
Who's this guy?

77
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:31,737
Well, the anonymous tip says…

78
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:34,657
Never mind.

79
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:35,992
Why'd you just stop?

80
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:39,203
- Hey, what case is this?
- A homeless man was found dead.

81
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:41,372
Apparently,
he sat in that corner for two days.

82
00:09:41,455 --> 00:09:42,915
No signs of foul play.

83
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:45,960
But we can't identify him.
His fingerprints aren't in the system.

84
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:48,629
You can't identify him?

85
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:50,923
All right. That's enough.

86
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:53,801
Lots of unclaimed remains these days.
No need to spell it out.

87
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,219
Oh.

88
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:56,721
Go ahead. Take him.

89
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:00,266
Once we're done here,

90
00:10:00,349 --> 00:10:02,935
let's go to this
great hangover soup spot nearby.

91
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:05,271
- It's on me. Let's go.
- Sounds good.

92
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,483
Hey.

93
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:12,820
You'd better treat your wife right. See?

94
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:16,115
That's what happens
when you've got no family.

95
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,533
Don't wait until she's gone.

96
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,627
What's with that look?

97
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:28,878
Gonna hit me or what?

98
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:30,630
Hey! Take the advice!

99
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:32,298
We're done here. Let's go now.

100
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:33,507
For fuck's sake.

101
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:36,594
- All right. Let's go!
- What a clown.

102
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:42,433
It's always your big mouth.
You just don't get it, you bastard!

103
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:43,726
- Mr. Park!
- Dong-cheol!

104
00:10:43,809 --> 00:10:44,644
- Let go!
- One sec!

105
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,686
- Let go!
- Don't!

106
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,188
- Son of a bitch!
- Bring it!

107
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:48,731
- Let's do this!
- You bastard.

108
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:50,775
- That's enough!
- Seriously!

109
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:52,068
Dong-cheol! Let's go!

110
00:10:52,151 --> 00:10:53,361
Let go of me!

111
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:57,698
<i>You idiot.</i>

112
00:10:57,782 --> 00:10:59,909
<i>Fighting at the scene? With a colleague?</i>

113
00:10:59,992 --> 00:11:01,577
<i>What, you've given up on life?</i>

114
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:03,412
<i>Gone off the rails, have you?!</i>

115
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:06,415
<i>Just close out that tip!</i>

116
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,375
<i>Hang up!</i>

117
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,799
Fuck, I should just quit.

118
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:03,222
SEOUL DONGBU POLICE STATION
PARK SUN-YONG

119
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:12,440
- Let's begin.
- Deal the cards already.

120
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,150
Here comes the river.

121
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:16,193
Let's see the cards.

122
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:17,945
Straight. Winning hand.

123
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:18,863
Raise.

124
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:21,657
- Place your bets.
- Just one more.

125
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:22,783
100,000 won.

126
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:24,493
No more bets.

127
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,829
- Call.
- Show your hand.

128
00:12:29,957 --> 00:12:31,709
I'll sort out your chips.

129
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,421
Showdown. Pair.

130
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:36,756
Drinks are on you tonight.

131
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:52,313
What?

132
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:55,608
What, I can't even look at you?

133
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:05,826
See the news?

134
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:08,621
What news?

135
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:12,833
The woman they found in the Hangang River.
The unidentified body.

136
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,211
No.

137
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:18,088
That passes for news these days?

138
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:20,716
You know that's ours, right?

139
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:23,344
Is it?

140
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:27,723
The fuck you mean?
Every item in that morgue is ours.

141
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:30,142
Oh, so that was ours.

142
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:38,776
Here's the thing.

143
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,445
A tip made it to the cops.

144
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:45,658
Fuck, this might turn into a headache.

145
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:48,828
Did you hear anything?

146
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,413
A tip? No.

147
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:05,636
Fuck.

148
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:07,763
You look pretty relaxed.

149
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:09,640
Like you have no idea.

150
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,895
Fine, then.

151
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:17,523
But, hey,

152
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:21,402
that look better not change.

153
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:22,862
Or you'll be in trouble.

154
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:24,154
You know that, right?

155
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:00,649
Fuck.

156
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:06,614
If the pigs get their hands on Noja,
they'll find out about all our jobs.

157
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:10,242
We gotta take out the fucking bastard
who sent that tip.

158
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,870
I don't think
it was Myeong-su, that asshole.

159
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:17,875
It's gotta be someone
who knows our operation inside out.

160
00:15:19,084 --> 00:15:21,754
Hey. Keep an eye on Noja.

161
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:24,214
If he gets busted,
we're gonna have to run.

162
00:15:24,882 --> 00:15:25,883
Yes, sir.

163
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:28,427
By the way, what's that smell?

164
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:31,305
- I loaded an item in the trunk.
- You…

165
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,390
Goddamn it.

166
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:35,684
Is the item done?

167
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:37,227
Yes, sir.

168
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:39,730
The car's gonna stink now, you fucking…

169
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,315
Just go.

170
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:02,419
I just have to talk to him for a moment.

171
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:03,796
Could you open the door?

172
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:06,173
Soo-hyun! Let's talk for a second.

173
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:08,884
<i>You've got the wrong place.</i>
<i>There's no one by that name.</i>

174
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:12,096
I checked it already.
Son Soo-hyun lives here!

175
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:15,057
<i>Whoever that is, they don't live here!</i>

176
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:17,267
<i>We've lived here for six years!</i>

177
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:19,770
<i>Where's the security guard?</i>
<i>Did you even call him?</i>

178
00:16:19,853 --> 00:16:22,773
<i>What's he doing?</i>
<i>He should be stopping people like him.</i>

179
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,276
PROFESSOR PARK GEUN-YEONG

180
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:30,406
PARK GEUN-YEONG

181
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:32,950
PROFESSOR PARK GEUN-YEONG

182
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,246
PROFESSOR PARK GEUN-YEONG

183
00:16:58,892 --> 00:16:59,935
You there!

184
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:02,146
This bastard was here, right?

185
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:05,232
4,500 won at 10:32!

186
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:06,650
Americano!

187
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:08,819
Well…

188
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:12,406
Yes, well… Earlier… Takeout…

189
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,116
A cup of Americano…

190
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:15,701
You sure it was him?

191
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,039
What the hell?

192
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,084
Why's this bastard acting up
all of a sudden?

193
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:58,410
Hey, Moon-jae.

194
00:17:58,494 --> 00:17:59,703
- <i>Hey, where are you?</i>
- Well…

195
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:02,206
I'm near the café.

196
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:03,165
<i>Already?</i>

197
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:07,836
<i>Noja's faster than I thought,</i>
<i>even in that piece of junk.</i>

198
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:10,339
Where are you?

199
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:12,299
<i>Maybe he's lost it.</i>
<i>He's at the Hangang River.</i>

200
00:18:12,382 --> 00:18:13,467
<i>Might kill himself.</i>

201
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:15,427
I don't think he can.

202
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:17,888
He can't go in the water.
He's afraid of it.

203
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:22,142
Moon-jae.

204
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:24,645
How long do I have to follow this guy?

205
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:26,021
<i>Let's see.</i>

206
00:18:26,522 --> 00:18:28,107
<i>Until I tell you to stop?</i>

207
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:30,025
<i>I told you.</i>

208
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:32,986
<i>Let him be chased,</i>
<i>but don't let him get caught.</i>

209
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:36,782
<i>If he dies, where's the fun in that?</i>
<i>Still a long way to go.</i>

210
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:38,575
<i>Call me when you're at the river.</i>

211
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:26,915
Who are you?

212
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:31,378
Can I help you?

213
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:33,755
You know me?

214
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:35,549
No.

215
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:36,758
Then why follow me?

216
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:38,719
I was following you?

217
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:40,971
You've been following me from the café.

218
00:19:55,485 --> 00:19:57,279
I wasn't following you.

219
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:02,367
This street is a dead end.

220
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:08,582
You're right. It is.

221
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:10,542
I'm not familiar with this area.

222
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:13,378
I thought this would lead out
if I kept going.

223
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:16,798
I figured since you came this way.

224
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:21,428
I'm sorry.

225
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:24,014
- Okay? Are we done?
- You little…

226
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:25,515
I'm sorry.

227
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,598
That thug's money is dirty anyway.

228
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:09,476
I'll launder it. I'll handle everything.

229
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:12,896
You just need to do a few things for me.

230
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:16,942
A fresh start for a thug? As if.

231
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:19,528
This is basically free money.

232
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:24,783
He can't even report it to the police.

233
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:27,786
What if I get caught?

234
00:21:30,205 --> 00:21:31,665
How would he catch you?

235
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:36,545
You'll disappear without a trace.
He'll never find you.

236
00:21:36,628 --> 00:21:39,548
Stop worrying. I'll take care of you.

237
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:43,010
I'm the only family you've got, punk.

238
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:45,721
Aren't I?

239
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,056
So help me out.

240
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:49,558
About

241
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:51,560
10% of the money?

242
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:53,729
<i>Okay?</i>

243
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:30,015
- <i>You knew, didn't you?</i>
- <i>No skid marks either.</i>

244
00:22:30,098 --> 00:22:32,225
- <i>It wasn't an accident.</i>
- <i>You knew, didn't you?</i>

245
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:43,487
<i>You're going through a lot for your age.</i>

246
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:45,530
<i>Do you have any other relatives?</i>

247
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:50,160
I always told you.

248
00:22:50,243 --> 00:22:52,954
You have to be a better Je Moon-jae
than the old Moon-jae.

249
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:54,706
Always remember that, okay?

250
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:58,043
You must've hated your dad too.
But don't worry anymore.

251
00:22:58,126 --> 00:23:01,380
He can't do anything to you now.

252
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:06,718
What are you talking about, Mom?
I hated you even more than him.

253
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:10,430
Your depression drove me crazy too.

254
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:13,600
He thinks he's hiding in there.
Doesn't even know he's trapped.

255
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:16,603
Who the hell are you? You bastards!

256
00:23:45,298 --> 00:23:46,925
It's your fault.

257
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:50,720
This is all your fault.

258
00:23:50,804 --> 00:23:51,805
What…

